;; The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until
;; the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops
;; it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,
;; else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it.



